# Command fnm — REMOVED, use mise

## What does this command do:

Nothing. **fnm is not installed and must not be reinstalled.**

Removed 2026-08-02 — the binary, its Node versions, and the shell fragment
`~/.bash.d/23_bashrc_fedora_fnm`, whose `fnm env --use-on-cd` loaded after `03_mise` and beat
the mise shims in `PATH`. `~/ai/directives/when-building-or-scaffolding-code-in-a-git-repo.md`
names **mise** the single tool version manager and forbids `fnm` by name.

## Command path

None. `command -v fnm` returns nothing, by design.

## Command documentation

Run **`cheat mise`** — it covers every command below and uses node as its worked example
throughout. See also `~/.bash.d/RUNBOOK.md`.

## Command options

# fnm -> mise, the ones worth memorising:

fnm install 22          ->  mise install node@22
fnm use 22              ->  mise use node@22        # writes ./mise.toml
fnm default 22          ->  mise use -g node@22     # writes ~/.config/mise/config.toml
fnm list                ->  mise ls node
fnm current             ->  mise current node
fnm uninstall 20        ->  mise uninstall node@20

# Auto-switch on cd needed `--use-on-cd` under fnm. mise does it natively via
# `mise activate` in ~/.bash.d/03_mise — nothing to add.

# Do NOT create .node-version or .nvmrc; both are forbidden. Pin in mise.toml.
